Krita Nova 37 - the text tool's options bar (text tool, part 2)

Like Photoshop's options bar, the text tool's Tool Options now start with:
font family, style, size, align left / center / right, text color, and
buttons that show the Character and Paragraph panels. It edits the same text
as the Character panel (patch 36): the selected characters while some are
selected, otherwise the whole text (or the defaults for new text). It flows
into as many rows as it needs, so it fits the Tool Options docker as well as
the tool options toolbar. Krita's own text tool options stay below it.

- qml/NovaTextOptionsBar.qml (text properties docker plugin): the bar.
- NovaTextPanelDock: canvasObserver property (the panel's text property
  models) and showPanel(id), for the bar.
- SvgTextToolOptions.qml: loads the bar at the top when the tool gives it the
  Character panel's observer; SvgTextTool::createOptionWidget() does that
  when the Character panel (NovaTextCharacter) exists.
